        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-asset" data-main="settings" data-sub="asset">
            <div class="info" style="border-left:4px solid #fd7e14;">
                <strong>This is the only place where this plugin sends data OFF the server.</strong>
                Everything else (scanning, inventory, CVE matching, reports, CSV) stays local - this connector
                forwards the lists you already have to an external asset-management system, and only when you
                deliberately configure a target and switch it on. It is <strong>disabled by default</strong> and
                there is no automatic push unless you set a sync interval below.
                <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li>The endpoint must be <strong>https</strong> - credentials never travel in the clear.</li>
                    <li>What leaves: the device identity (name, group, OS), the hardware identifiers, the
                        installed-software list and the vulnerability findings of each pushed device - i.e. the
                        same data the CSV export contains.</li>
                    <li>Credentials are stored in <code>scanner-settings.json</code> on this server, are
                        <strong>never shown back in the clear</strong> and are <strong>never written to a log</strong>;
                        the log records only device, HTTP status and an external id.</li>
                    <li>The push runs entirely server-side from stored inventory: it sends
                        <strong>no command to any agent</strong> and never touches a device.</li>
                </ul>
                Choose <em>Generic</em> for any REST system (a JSON body template with placeholders), or use the
                built-in presets for <strong>Jira</strong> (one issue per device) and <strong>Snipe-IT</strong>
                (one hardware asset per device). Both create on the first push and update on later pushes.
            </div>

            <h3>Target</h3>
            <div class="setgrid">
                <label for="asEnabled">Enable asset sync</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="asEnabled">
                    <div class="hint">Master switch. Off by default; nothing is sent until it is on AND a target is configured.</div></div>

                <label for="asTargetType">Target system</label>
                <div><select id="asTargetType">
                        <option value="generic">Generic REST (JSON body template)</option>
                        <option value="jira">Jira (issue per device)</option>
                        <option value="snipeit">Snipe-IT (hardware asset per device)</option>
                    </select></div>

                <label for="asEndpointUrl">Endpoint URL (https)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="asEndpointUrl" style="width:420px" placeholder="https://assets.example.com">
                    <div class="hint">Generic: the exact URL to POST to. Jira: the base URL (e.g. https://yourcompany.atlassian.net).
                    Snipe-IT: the base URL (e.g. https://snipe.example.com).</div></div>

                <label for="asAuthMode">Authentication</label>
                <div><select id="asAuthMode">
                        <option value="none">none</option>
                        <option value="bearer">Bearer token</option>
                        <option value="basic">Basic (user + password/API token)</option>
                        <option value="header">Custom header</option>
                    </select></div>

                <label for="asUsername">Username</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="asUsername" style="width:300px">
                    <div class="hint">For Basic auth (Jira Cloud: your account e-mail).</div></div>

                <label for="asToken">Token</label>
                <div><input type="password" id="asToken" style="width:300px" autocomplete="new-password">
                    <label style="font-weight:400;"><input type="checkbox" id="asClearToken"> clear the stored token</label>
                    <div class="hint" id="asTokenHint">Stored secrets are never displayed. Leave blank to keep the stored value; tick "clear" to erase it.</div></div>

                <label for="asPassword">Password / API token</label>
                <div><input type="password" id="asPassword" style="width:300px" autocomplete="new-password">
                    <label style="font-weight:400;"><input type="checkbox" id="asClearPassword"> clear the stored password</label></div>

                <label for="asHeaderName">Custom header name</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="asHeaderName" style="width:300px" placeholder="X-Api-Key"></div>

                <label for="asHeaderValue">Custom header value</label>
                <div><input type="password" id="asHeaderValue" style="width:300px" autocomplete="new-password">
                    <label style="font-weight:400;"><input type="checkbox" id="asClearHeaderValue"> clear the stored value</label></div>

                <label for="asOnly">Which devices to push</label>
                <div><select id="asOnly">
                        <option value="all">All devices</option>
                        <option value="vulnerable">Only devices with vulnerabilities</option>
                    </select></div>

                <label for="asIntervalHours">Automatic sync every (hours)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="asIntervalHours" class="num" value="0">
                    <div class="hint">0 = no automatic push (on-demand only). Otherwise the server pushes on this cycle.</div></div>
            </div>

            <div id="asGenericFields">
                <h3>Generic REST mapping</h3>
                <div class="setgrid">
                    <label for="asMethod">HTTP method</label>
                    <div><select id="asMethod">
                            <option value="POST">POST</option><option value="PUT">PUT</option><option value="PATCH">PATCH</option>
                        </select></div>
                    <label for="asHeadersJson">Extra headers (JSON object)</label>
                    <div><textarea id="asHeadersJson" rows="3" style="width:520px;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;">{}</textarea></div>
                    <label for="asBodyTemplate">Body template (JSON)</label>
                    <div><textarea id="asBodyTemplate" rows="12" style="width:620px;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;"></textarea>
                        <div class="hint" id="asTemplateHint"></div></div>
                    <label for="asExternalIdPath">External id in the answer</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asExternalIdPath" style="width:260px" placeholder="id">
                        <div class="hint">Where the target returns its own id (a dotted path, e.g. <code>id</code> or
                        <code>data.asset.id</code>). Stored per device so the next push UPDATES that record instead
                        of creating a duplicate. Leave empty if the target has no such id.</div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div id="asJiraFields" style="display:none;">
                <h3>Jira</h3>
                <div class="setgrid">
                    <label for="asJiraProject">Project key</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asJiraProject" style="width:160px" placeholder="IT"></div>
                    <label for="asJiraIssueType">Issue type</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asJiraIssueType" style="width:200px" value="Task"></div>
                    <label for="asJiraLabel">Label</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asJiraLabel" style="width:220px" value="inventory-scanner">
                        <div class="hint">Used to recognise issues this plugin created.</div></div>
                    <label for="asJiraSummary">Summary template</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asJiraSummary" style="width:420px"></div>
                    <label for="asJiraVulnIssues">Also one issue per vulnerability</label>
                    <div><input type="checkbox" id="asJiraVulnIssues">
                        <div class="hint">Off: one issue per device carrying all three lists. On: additionally one issue per finding.</div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div id="asSnipeFields" style="display:none;">
                <h3>Snipe-IT</h3>
                <div class="setgrid">
                    <label for="asSnipeNameTemplate">Asset name template</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asSnipeNameTemplate" style="width:420px"></div>
                    <label for="asSnipeCategory">Category id (optional)</label>
                    <div><input type="text" id="asSnipeCategory" class="num">
                        <div class="hint">Numeric Snipe-IT category id; leave empty for none.</div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="controls" style="margin-top:14px;">
                <button id="asSaveBtn" data-help="as.save">Save configuration</button>
                <button id="asTestBtn" data-help="as.test">Send a test request</button>
                <button class="green" id="asPushAllBtn" data-help="as.pushall">Push all devices now</button>
                <span id="asRunInfo" class="hint"></span>
            </div>
            <div id="asMsg"></div>

            <h3>Last push per device</h3>
            <div class="table-container">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Group</th><th style="width:190px;">Last push</th><th style="width:90px;">Status</th><th style="width:80px;">HTTP</th><th style="width:150px;">External id</th><th style="width:90px;"></th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody id="asStatusBody"><tr><td colspan="7" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h3>Asset sync log</h3>
            <div><button id="asRefreshLogBtn" class="small">Refresh log</button> <span id="asLogInfo" class="hint"></span></div>
            <pre id="asLog" style="max-height:220px;overflow:auto;background:#0f1720;color:#cfe3f5;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11px;margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;">(not loaded yet)</pre>
        </div>
